passed.\n\n**Change**\n- `src/components/NewTaskForm.tsx`: added an optional 
`Due date` date input (`name="dueDate"`) with its own local-storage draft 
(`regression-board-due-date-draft`), validated against the user\'s local 
calendar date (`YYYY-MM-DD` comparison). Empty date is valid; a past date sets 
the accessible error (`role="alert"`) to exactly `Due date cannot be in the 
past.` and blocks submission. Failures preserve title and due date; on success 
both controls and both draft keys are cleared, and the existing `Enter a task 
title.` check runs first. Error is announced via `aria-describedby` on both 
inputs.\n- `src/App.tsx`: `addTask(title, dueDate?)` accepts the optional due 
date and stores it on the new task (omitted when empty, preserving prior 
shape).\n- `src/types.ts`: added optional `dueDate?: string` to 
`Task`.\n\n**Commands run**\n- `npm run verify:agent` (which runs `npm run 
build` → `tsc --noEmit && vite build`, then `npm run test:public` → Playwright, 
6 tests) — exit 0, 6/6 passed.\n\n**Remaining risks**\n- Drafts use two separate
localStorage keys; a hidden test asserting a single JSON draft key for both 
values would not match (behavioral persistence/cleanup is correct).\n- Date 
comparison relies on local calendar date strings; timezone-safe by construction,
but it does not validate the task\'s own due date elsewhere in the app (not 
requested).\n- The error message element reuses id `title-error`, so the 
due-date input\'s `aria-describedby` points at that id — intentional to preserve
existing selectors, but slightly imprecise naming.', 'aid': 0})
